For the action $D_(2n) arrow.cw.half X_n$ on the vertices of a regular $n$-gon, an orbit has size $n$ and a vertex stabiliser has size $2$, giving $abs(D_(2n)) = 2n$.

For the isometry group of a cube acting on face centres, an orbit has size $6$ and a face stabiliser has size $8$, giving $abs(G) = 6 times 8 = 48$.
